{
  "__comment": "NVisionX Backup Status — ALL EKS CLIENTS, ONE DASHBOARD. Same layout pattern as scan-activity-all-clients.json (combined overview + one collapsible row per client). CONFIRMED LIVE against Integration (2026-08-19): kube_job_status_succeeded/_failed/_completion_time/_start_time are USELESS here - both backup CronJobs set ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 600, so kube-state-metrics only ever sees the completed Job object for a 10-minute window after each run (daily for postgres, weekly for opensearch); outside that window the query returns nothing at all, which is what 'No data' on the first version of this dashboard actually meant. Rebuilt around kube_cronjob_status_last_successful_time instead, which lives on the permanent CronJob object (never garbage-collected) - confirmed present with real values: cronjob='databases-postgres-backup' (namespace default, schedule '0 2 * * *' daily) and cronjob='databases-opensearch-backup' (schedule '0 2 * * 0' weekly). Health per client = freshness of that timestamp vs. 1.5x the expected schedule interval (36h for daily postgres, 216h/9d for weekly opensearch) - a generous grace window, not exact-schedule matching, since exact run time can drift a little run to run. Per-run duration and multi-run history panels were dropped entirely rather than shipped broken - that data doesn't survive the Job's 10-minute TTL and there is no CronJob-level substitute for it.",
